    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 27 Clarinda Park West is a home full of character and ready for its next chapter! There is something particularly appealing about a house that gives you the opportunity to start afresh while already possessing so much of what cannot be recreated. Tucked away on Clarinda Park West, this gracious terraced period home is a wonderful example of the elegant houses that give this part of Dún Laoghaire its enduring appeal. This is very much a house to make your own. It does not demand that everything be tackled at once; rather, it offers the freedom to live in it, understand the spaces and gradually bring your own ideas to life. The period bones are already here — what happens next is entirely up to you.\n\nBehind the neat railed front garden lies a surprisingly bright and characterful interior, where tall ceilings, sliding sash windows, working shutters, stained glass, original fireplaces and beautifully detailed plasterwork remain largely intact. The entrance hall sets the scene beautifully, with glazing around the front door drawing natural light deep into the house and an elaborate ceiling rose and intricate coving immediately catching the eye. The accommodation unfolds over three levels, with two reception rooms at ground floor level, a kitchen and ancillary rooms on the return, and a generous arrangement of bedrooms, bathrooms. There is also plenty of scope to rethink the layout for your own living needs, subject to the necessary permissions. To the rear of the house, there is a paved garden, ready and waiting for a green thumbed owner to work their magic and create a private oasis of calm and tranquillity.\n\nAnd then there is the setting. Clarinda Park West is particularly well positioned, just a short stroll from the centre of Dún Laoghaire, the park itself is on the doorstep, and cafés, restaurants, independent shops and DART all within easy reach, along with the boutique villages of Galsthule and Monkstown, that bookend the locality. The local coastline and harbour are also just a short 7 minute walk away. There are an excellent selection of transport links that serve the area including the Dart, numerous popular bus routes and the Aircoach providing swift ease of access to the airport. Local educational facilities are also in abundance with a number of highly regarded schools close by, IADT on Kill Avenue and further third level educational facilities along the Dart line and bus routes."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall Floor - \n\n\nEntrance hall: - 4.90m x 1.84m\ntall ceilings with intricate coving and centre rose, hall door flanked by glazed surround, door to rear garden\n\nGuest w.c.: - \nw.c., w.h.b.,\n\nDrawing Room: - 4.86m x 4.71m\nbeautifully appointed, light filled, tall ceiling with ceiling coving and centre rose, feature fireplace with tiled inset, sliding sash window with stained glass inset, working window shutters, archway set into wall that adjoins the dining room\n\nDining Room: - 4.55m x 4.19m\ngenerously appointed, working window shutters, feature fireplace with tiled inset and brass hood, ceiling coving and archway set into the wall that adjoins the drawing room\n\nKitchen: - 4.06m x 3.42m\nfitted units with electric hob, cast iron feature fireplace.\n\nPantry: - 2.14m x 1.83m\nwith window and fitted shelving\n\nUtility Room: - 1.83m x 1.23m\nwith fitted storage, tiled splashback, washing machine, dryer, recessed lighting\n\nReturn - \n\n\nWC: - 1.82m x 1.27m\nw.c., w.h.b.\n\nBedroom 3: - 3.50m x 3.40m\ncurrently set up as a kitchen/living, with fitted units, stainless steel sink, electric hob, feature fireplace, door through to dressing room attic access and en-suite\n\nEn-Suite: - 1.83m x 0.64m\nw.c., w.h.b., step in shower cubicle\n\nFirst floor - \n\n\nLanding: - 5.73m x 2.01m\nceiling coving, roof light\n\nBedroom 2: - 4.71m x 4.19m max\nvery generously appointed, working window shutters, feature fireplace, access into a w.c. en-suite\n\nEn-suite: - \nw.c. and w.h.b.\n\nBedroom 1: - 4.86m x 3.76m\nextraordinarily bright, sliding sash window with working window shutters, very tall ceiling, feature marble fireplace with tiled inset\n\nBathroom: - 3.87m x 2.79m\nsliding sash window with working window shutters feature fireplace, bath, sink, step in shower cubicle, hot press, attic access\n\nTop return - \n\n\nLobby: - \nfitted wall and floor units, electric hob, stainless steel sink, fridge/freezer, recessed lighting.\n\nDressing Room: - \nwith window\n\nBedroom 4: - 3.56m x 2.44m\nfeature fireplace, working window shutters\n\nShower Room: - 2.00m x 0.66m\nw.c., w.h.b., step in shower cubicle\n\nGarden - \nTo the front of the house there is a neat, railed and pebbled garden. There is a paved low maintenance garden to the rear.\n\n"
